<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.12 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 22.12 percent at an auction on April 15 from 23.19 at the last auction on April 8, the Kazakhstan National Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The following details of the auction were provided --</p>
<p>					  April 15	    April 8</p>
<p> Series number		  KZ43K1707977     KZ43K1007972</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	     500		 500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	    1,2		1,68</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	    500		 500</p>
<p> Average price (pct)		     94.76	     94.52</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)		     22.12	     23.19</p>
<p> Tenor (days)				91		  91</p>
<p> Maturity			     July 17, 1997    July 10, 1997</p>
<p>The finance ministry is also auctioning 500 million tenge of three-month bills on April 22.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
